1
00:00:00,880 --> 00:00:04,845
A flagged transaction is the start of an investigation.

2
00:00:04,880 --> 00:00:09,885
Which account needs attention, what happened, and which policy applies?

3
00:00:09,920 --> 00:00:12,005
At Meridian Demo Bank, we'll use

4
00:00:12,040 --> 00:00:15,565
Oracle AI Data Platform to connect transaction

5
00:00:15,600 --> 00:00:19,445
data, policy documents and specialist agents.

6
00:00:19,480 --> 00:00:21,805
Then we'll bring the investigation copilot

7
00:00:21,840 --> 00:00:24,395
to users in Agent Hub and Streamlit.

8
00:00:26,390 --> 00:00:28,185
Before an agent can answer those

9
00:00:28,220 --> 00:00:31,675
questions, it needs a useful data foundation.

10
00:00:31,710 --> 00:00:38,435
In Workbench, the Spark notebook organizes transactions into Bronze, Silver and Gold.

11
00:00:38,470 --> 00:00:41,035
Bronze keeps the incoming records.

12
00:00:41,070 --> 00:00:44,875
Silver validates them and adds time features.

13
00:00:44,910 --> 00:00:49,595
Gold prepares account-month analytics and transaction-level features.

14
00:00:49,630 --> 00:00:52,815
A separate random forest exercise shows how those

15
00:00:52,850 --> 00:00:56,555
features can support model training and evaluation.

16
00:00:56,590 --> 00:01:00,635
The investigation queue in this demo uses screening rules.

17
00:01:00,670 --> 00:01:06,475
We publish the Gold tables into Autonomous AI Lakehouse for executive analytics.

18
00:01:06,510 --> 00:01:11,435
Catalog, schema and table definitions remain configurable.

19
00:01:11,470 --> 00:01:16,876
The agent's SQL tools query prepared Spark serving tables derived from Gold.

20
00:01:18,920 --> 00:01:21,035
The dashboards give us the portfolio

21
00:01:21,070 --> 00:01:24,565
picture before we open an individual account.

22
00:01:24,600 --> 00:01:32,205
The notebook and Oracle Analytics show activity, screening flags, exposure and concentration.

23
00:01:32,240 --> 00:01:36,125
The investigation queue turns a broad portfolio signal

24
00:01:36,160 --> 00:01:38,680
into a short list for analyst review.

25
00:01:38,900 --> 00:01:43,005
Trends and exposure breakdowns add context: is the

26
00:01:43,040 --> 00:01:49,125
activity concentrated in particular accounts, transaction types or locations?

27
00:01:49,160 --> 00:01:51,680
That is the handoff to the copilot.

28
00:01:51,920 --> 00:01:54,425
Take a focused question beyond the chart, and

29
00:01:54,460 --> 00:01:57,344
retrieve the records and policy behind it.

30
00:01:59,380 --> 00:02:01,915
In Agent Builder, the flow starts with a

31
00:02:01,950 --> 00:02:06,465
message, a guardrails node and the investigation supervisor.

32
00:02:06,500 --> 00:02:11,305
The supervisor interprets the request and coordinates four specialists.

33
00:02:11,340 --> 00:02:14,175
The portfolio SQL agent retrieves reporting

34
00:02:14,210 --> 00:02:18,985
context, monthly totals, trends and exposure mix.

35
00:02:19,020 --> 00:02:22,050
The investigation SQL agent retrieves ranked

36
00:02:22,360 --> 00:02:26,105
accounts, an account snapshot and transaction evidence.

37
00:02:26,140 --> 00:02:31,785
Seven predefined SQL tools keep aggregation and ranking in the data layer.

38
00:02:31,820 --> 00:02:36,945
We can inspect a tool's query, input parameters and test result.

39
00:02:36,980 --> 00:02:41,745
This makes the connection between a business question and its data explicit.

40
00:02:41,780 --> 00:02:45,425
The policy agent searches a curated knowledge base.

41
00:02:45,460 --> 00:02:49,435
Its RAG tool retrieves relevant passages and source

42
00:02:49,470 --> 00:02:54,385
references, adding business context alongside the structured evidence.

43
00:02:54,420 --> 00:02:57,455
The brief agent uses a Prompt tool to organize

44
00:02:57,490 --> 00:03:01,825
the supplied facts and passages into an analyst draft.

45
00:03:01,860 --> 00:03:07,665
It is configured to preserve scope, show tables and identify missing information.

46
00:03:07,700 --> 00:03:10,505
The value comes from coordination.

47
00:03:10,540 --> 00:03:13,560
Each specialist has a clear role, and the supervisor

48
00:03:13,880 --> 00:03:17,539
brings the required contributions back to the user's question.

49
00:03:19,880 --> 00:03:23,325
Let's start in the playground with a portfolio question.

50
00:03:23,360 --> 00:03:26,505
The response returns the reporting month, transaction

51
00:03:26,540 --> 00:03:29,765
activity and flagged exposure in a table.

52
00:03:29,800 --> 00:03:33,165
The source and reporting scope stay with the answer.

53
00:03:33,200 --> 00:03:37,365
Next, we ask for the complete priority-one policy.

54
00:03:37,400 --> 00:03:42,645
The policy agent retrieves the threshold conditions and cites the document.

55
00:03:42,680 --> 00:03:47,005
Those conditions explain how an account enters the review queue.

56
00:03:47,040 --> 00:03:51,685
Now we investigate the account with the highest flagged exposure.

57
00:03:51,720 --> 00:03:55,495
The draft separates account totals from supporting transactions,

58
00:03:55,530 --> 00:04:00,230
with amounts, dates, transaction types and screening scores.

59
00:04:00,320 --> 00:04:05,565
It also presents the relevant policy and proposed analyst review steps.

60
00:04:05,600 --> 00:04:08,355
This gives the investigator a starting point for

61
00:04:08,390 --> 00:04:11,845
review, while the underlying records remain essential.

62
00:04:11,880 --> 00:04:15,765
A fluent draft still needs checking against its sources.

63
00:04:15,800 --> 00:04:19,100
Testing matters at each layer: the SQL tool

64
00:04:19,280 --> 00:04:24,245
result, the retrieved policy passage, and the combined response.

65
00:04:24,280 --> 00:04:27,205
Focused follow-ups help us inspect the evidence

66
00:04:27,240 --> 00:04:29,045
and check what the agent can actually

67
00:04:29,080 --> 00:04:31,981
support before making it available to users.

68
00:04:35,890 --> 00:04:40,495
After testing, the workflow is deployed on AI compute.

69
00:04:40,530 --> 00:04:43,575
The Agent Card describes what the copilot can do,

70
00:04:43,610 --> 00:04:47,660
with a version, a clear description and example questions.

71
00:04:47,930 --> 00:04:52,570
Here, four skills cover portfolio analytics, account triage

72
00:04:52,730 --> 00:04:57,655
and transaction evidence, policy retrieval, and investigation briefing.

73
00:04:57,690 --> 00:05:02,775
Those skill descriptions help people understand when to use the agent.

74
00:05:02,810 --> 00:05:06,635
Registering the deployed agent in AI Registry makes

75
00:05:06,670 --> 00:05:11,695
those capabilities discoverable, subject to its access permissions.

76
00:05:11,730 --> 00:05:15,760
The deployment provides an endpoint for applications to call.

77
00:05:15,970 --> 00:05:19,335
The card and registry connect that running workflow

78
00:05:19,370 --> 00:05:22,173
with the users and applications that need it.

79
00:05:24,380 --> 00:05:27,290
In Agent Hub, users can find the copilot

80
00:05:27,380 --> 00:05:30,185
and ask a question without opening the builder.

81
00:05:30,220 --> 00:05:33,295
Here, a focused follow-up asks for the current

82
00:05:33,330 --> 00:05:37,065
transaction evidence behind an account's screening totals.

83
00:05:37,100 --> 00:05:41,185
The response shows the supporting rows and policy context.

84
00:05:41,220 --> 00:05:44,425
This is where the analyst can inspect dates, amounts

85
00:05:44,460 --> 00:05:48,385
and scores, rather than relying on a summary alone.

86
00:05:48,420 --> 00:05:51,202
The output remains a draft for human review.

87
00:05:57,400 --> 00:06:02,685
The same deployed workflow can also sit behind a local Streamlit application.

88
00:06:02,720 --> 00:06:04,635
The application connects to the agent

89
00:06:04,670 --> 00:06:08,785
endpoint and presents a focused copilot interface.

90
00:06:08,820 --> 00:06:12,095
Here, we review portfolio activity, then ask

91
00:06:12,130 --> 00:06:15,885
which accounts have the highest flagged exposure.

92
00:06:15,920 --> 00:06:17,495
The answer comes back as a

93
00:06:17,530 --> 00:06:21,085
readable table, with source and scope information.

94
00:06:21,120 --> 00:06:25,525
The investigation capability stays with the deployed agent.

95
00:06:25,560 --> 00:06:29,345
The application controls how people interact with it.

96
00:06:29,380 --> 00:06:32,585
This brings connected data and policy context into

97
00:06:32,620 --> 00:06:36,270
an interface an analyst can use, while leaving

98
00:06:36,330 --> 00:06:39,748
the decision about further investigation with the analyst.

99
00:06:41,880 --> 00:06:45,975
We've connected a prepared data foundation, executive analytics

100
00:06:46,010 --> 00:06:50,285
and specialist agents into one investigation experience.

101
00:06:50,320 --> 00:06:52,135
The aim is to reduce the effort

102
00:06:52,170 --> 00:06:54,585
of searching for records, finding the

103
00:06:54,620 --> 00:06:57,885
right policy and assembling a review draft.

104
00:06:57,920 --> 00:07:03,285
The notebooks, agent setup and application code are in the project repository.

105
00:07:03,320 --> 00:07:04,805
Start with a signal.

106
00:07:04,840 --> 00:07:06,525
Follow the evidence.

107
00:07:06,560 --> 00:07:08,510
Keep the analyst in control.
